 "result": "Fixed. In `src/click/_utils.py`, `Sentinel` members' enum values are plain `object()` instances, so the default `Enum.__reduce_ex__` (which reconstructs by value) fails identity/equality lookup during `pickle` and \u00e2\u20ac\u201d on Python versions without `Enum.__copy__`/`__deepcopy__` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d during `copy`/`deepcopy` too, raising `ValueError: ... is not a valid Sentinel`.\n\nAdded an `__reduce_ex__` override that reconstructs via `getattr(Sentinel, name)` instead, so `copy.copy`, `copy.deepcopy`, and `pickle.loads(pickle.dumps(...))` all return the same `UNSET`/`FLAG_NEEDS_VALUE` singleton. Verified with manual round-trip tests and the full test suite (all passing). Also added a CHANGES.md entry.",
